openassembler/emu/ops.py.doc:
Instruction semantics.

Integer semantics follow Mesa NAK's constant folder (nak/ir.rs `fold()`), which
upstream tests against hardware. Where NAK has no folder or the corpus uses a
form NAK doesn't model, the rule is marked HYPOTHESIS and must be confirmed by
the differential harness (tools/diff_emu.py) before it's relied on.

Handler kinds:
  @alu    per-thread, runs only where the guard is true; pc advances by 16
  @warp   gets every guard-true thread of the converged group at once
  @ctrl   per-thread, sets the thread's pc itself

symbols.doc:
Sum after aligning every term to the largest one and dropping bits more than
`bits` below its leading bit. trunc="rz": sign-magnitude truncation (toward 0);
trunc="floor": two's-complement right shift (toward -inf).

nvdisasm (sm_80) rejects no-yield (bit 109 = 1) with stall 0 or 12..15;
yield (bit 109 = 0) allows any stall. Measured by sweeping stall x bit 109
on 8 seeds of different opcodes.

arrays: param name -> initial bytes (each placed in its own window);
scalars: param name -> raw 32-bit value (f32 as bits). Returns (code, stats, [mismatch])
where a mismatch is (param, byte offset, ours, expected) per differing 32-bit word.

cmode="joint": c is one more term in the first block's alignment;
cmode="after": each block's products are aligned/summed alone, then added to the
running accumulator with a second aligned add.
